Proof lead
  1. Proper neighborhoods are pairwise disjoint at bounded span S=2q-1.
  2. Non-divisor G_P holes have a positive separation margin from every
     proper a/b neighborhood; only selected multiples of b matter.
  3. The proper residual is therefore the divisor-depth ledger above.
  4. The origin interval is a decoy: either p=1 is absent and origin mass
     survives, or p=1 is present and one P-slot is unavailable for the
     divisor-depth cover of b>=2.

